Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Introduction",
 FontSize->36,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.7607843137254902, 0.29411764705882354`, 0.08235294117647059]]], "Subtitle",\

 CellChangeTimes->{{3.89325259655807*^9, 3.893252598919417*^9}, {
  3.8932560720239463`*^9, 3.893256076743604*^9}, {3.893256115992225*^9, 
  3.893256116067061*^9}, {3.89772743676551*^9, 3.897727458937772*^9}, {
  3.937991997809936*^9, 3.937991998495105*^9}, {3.960899189472784*^9, 
  3.9608991906082134`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"172e8229-13ee-ae47-8d31-\
67b4f60e5b9d"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, we analyse a system of ODEs describing an FLRW universe \
with dark matter interacting with dark energy with a quadratic equation of \
state (EoS). The variables x, y and z in the ODEs are normalised, such that \
they are dimensionless, and correspond to: 

x - dark energy density,
y - Hubble expansion function,
z - dark matter energy density.

We complete a dynamical systems analysis of this model to understand whether \
we can avoid a singularity. In addition, we want to understand whether \
trajectories in the phase space have a decelerated era, and a late-time \
accelerated expansion, as qualitatively this is consistent with observations \
of our Universe. Ideally, we are looking for a parameter range where all \
trajectories avoid a singularity and have at least one decelerated expansion \
phase, for any initial condition.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9605388650218887`*^9, 3.960538867427691*^9}, {
  3.960541143499325*^9, 3.9605411506097736`*^9}, {3.960543108010094*^9, 
  3.960543136585682*^9}, {3.960544191311695*^9, 3.960544196417282*^9}, {
  3.960544527306427*^9, 3.960544528182106*^9}, {3.960558535470106*^9, 
  3.960558552778393*^9}, {3.960558725492396*^9, 3.960558792229702*^9}, {
  3.96055893920644*^9, 3.960558979271589*^9}, {3.960652487052265*^9, 
  3.960652515610855*^9}, {3.960653093001802*^9, 3.960653208212637*^9}, {
  3.9609025866897316`*^9, 
  3.9609026324196186`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"76f01345-1b48-674a-a199-\
54cd5d2e5658"]
}, Open  ]],

