Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Find the Parameter Space",
 FontSize->24,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[0]]], "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.900736651217819*^9, 3.900736670966432*^9}, {
  3.900736704428061*^9, 3.900736716758671*^9}, {3.9313435322951117`*^9, 
  3.931343553879564*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bfc498ea-0123-8d48-b694-\
495e051b2974"],

Cell["\<\
We want to find the parameter ranges for which we have a high energy \
repellor, as well as a low-energy attractor, such that trajectories emerge \
from a non-singular state, and tend towards a cosmological constant at low \
energy. In this section, we consider wx > -1 and wx < -1, for both \[Epsilon] \
= +1 and \[Epsilon] = -1. We then investigate the possible cases by varying q. 

In reality, we require 10^(-120) < \[ScriptCapitalR] < 10^(-60), which \
corresponds to trajectories emerging between Planck and inflationary scales, \
however we use a much larger value to produce readable phase spaces. In the \
end, the dynamics is unaffected by the value of \[ScriptCapitalR]; it only \
affects the position of the X = \[ScriptCapitalR]/(1+\[ScriptCapitalR]) (x = \
\[ScriptCapitalR]) fixed point.

We find that when w > -1 and \[Epsilon] = -1, we have a phase space where the \
X = 3/(3+q) (x = 3/q) fixed point is a repellor, and the X = \
\[ScriptCapitalR]/(1+\[ScriptCapitalR]) (x = \[ScriptCapitalR]) fixed point \
is an attractor. The fixed point at X = (1+wx)/(1+wx-\[Epsilon])(x = -(1+wx)/\
\[Epsilon]) is a saddle. Depending on the values of parameters within this \
range, we find that the repellor can either be a spiral repellor, a repelling \
node or an improper node. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.900737517566082*^9, 3.900737668417698*^9}, {
   3.900739582449397*^9, 3.900739681312413*^9}, {3.900740060735637*^9, 
   3.900740106006314*^9}, {3.921047321515623*^9, 3.921047322721915*^9}, {
   3.93134270593398*^9, 3.931342706327343*^9}, 3.931342993458527*^9, {
   3.941525033023599*^9, 3.9415250440060825`*^9}, {3.960661599342222*^9, 
   3.960661642882813*^9}, {3.960662061249284*^9, 3.960662180588135*^9}, {
   3.960662256010308*^9, 3.960662315127828*^9}, {3.960662462892498*^9, 
   3.960662537528604*^9}, {3.9609033246168423`*^9, 3.9609033620398617`*^9}, {
   3.960960107166918*^9, 3.9609601148263035`*^9}, {3.960960480770178*^9, 
   3.9609604811300507`*^9}, {3.96096056164526*^9, 
   3.9609606297735195`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a4d7fd4b-2bb3-6842-8b03-\
390f0d0ef8d5"],

