Cell[TextData[{
 "So, the fixed point at x = 3/q cannot be a repellor whilst the fixed point \
at x = \[ScriptCapitalR] is an attractor when \[Epsilon] = +1 and wx < -1. In \
general, the x = 3/q fixed point will not exist for z > 0 when the fixed \
point at x = \[ScriptCapitalR] is an attractor. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "-", "wx"}], "\[Epsilon]"]}], ")"}]], "Input",
  CellChangeTimes->{{3.898668334094038*^9, 3.898668361034275*^9}, {
    3.898668392850503*^9, 3.898668411913447*^9}, {3.898668454913151*^9, 
    3.898668462554039*^9}, {3.898668509873629*^9, 3.89866851064113*^9}, {
    3.898669207799498*^9, 3.898669251903385*^9}, {3.898672392826556*^9, 
    3.898672398505774*^9}, {3.900576616898684*^9, 3.9005766259608173`*^9}, {
    3.900581426053297*^9, 3.900581429241959*^9}, {3.900738340031426*^9, 
    3.900738348183306*^9}, {3.900738401887984*^9, 3.90073846805442*^9}, {
    3.900738942324915*^9, 3.90073894491651*^9}, {3.900739034405262*^9, 
    3.900739043771841*^9}, {3.900739528249945*^9, 3.900739554026325*^9}, {
    3.900750692805222*^9, 3.900750694452507*^9}, {3.90075073938088*^9, 
    3.900750770916634*^9}, {3.900751123043138*^9, 3.900751123434891*^9}, {
    3.900753452929438*^9, 3.900753477169083*^9}, {3.90075483869925*^9, 
    3.900754844465188*^9}, {3.900755059722123*^9, 3.900755064496393*^9}, 
    3.901344654250241*^9, {3.9013451530269423`*^9, 3.9013451613492727`*^9}, {
    3.918644311647399*^9, 3.9186443147667*^9}, 3.922437595449257*^9, 
    3.941523445598078*^9, {3.941523480340559*^9, 3.941523488028197*^9}, {
    3.9437915210950336`*^9, 3.943791541195335*^9}, {3.9458574249039364`*^9, 
    3.9458574315534086`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->
  "86bfef6e-b91a-e041-ba3b-b76248663efb"],
 " fixed point does have a larger x-coordinate than the attractor, however \
for these parameter ranges it cannot be a repellor."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9224373020181007`*^9, 3.922437397747277*^9}, {
