Cell["\<\
The x  = 3/q fixed point can be a repellor for z > 0 when the x = \
\[ScriptCapitalR]  fixed point is an attractor, but the stability of this \
fixed point changes depending on the combination of parameter constraints \
used: it can be a spiral repellor, a repelling node or an improper node. In \
general, there are a range of q values where both the x = \[ScriptCapitalR] \
and x = 3/q fixed point exist for x > 0 and z > 0, where the x = \
\[ScriptCapitalR] fixed point is an attractor, and the x = 3/q point is a \
(spiral) repellor.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.900738947486915*^9, 3.900739022043452*^9}, {
   3.9007479986093893`*^9, 3.900748003308853*^9}, {3.900748076464497*^9, 
   3.900748077391432*^9}, {3.900751255465028*^9, 3.900751323593565*^9}, 
