066abf92cc93"],

Cell["\<\
As before, we plot the 2D z - x dynamics, as well as the compact Z - X phase \
spaces, for wx > -1 and \[Epsilon] = -1. Y > 0 in these phase spaces, \
therefore the trajectories are expanding. We complete a dynamical systems \
analysis for each case when the repellor is a spiral repellor, a repelling \
node and improper node.   

We also plot the curve when the acceleration is zero (a\[CloseCurlyQuote]\
\[CloseCurlyQuote] = 0). If the separatrix and zero acceleration curve cross, \
then all trajectories have at least one decelerated phase. This subcase is of \
particular interest, as all trajectories are non-singular, and have at least \
one decelerated expansion phase for any initial condition. Trajectories which \
cross the zero acceleration curve four times have two decelerated phases, and \
those that cross twice have one. There is a limiting case where a trajectory \
first touches the zero acceleration curve, and then crosses it twice. 

If the separatrix and zero acceleration curve do not cross, some trajectories \
have one decelerated phase, and some always accelerate. There is a limiting \
case where a trajectory reaches a point of zero acceleration when it touches \
the zero acceleration curve, but otherwise accelerates. 

Finally, the separatrix and zero acceleration curve can touch. In this case, \
the separatrix itself is a trajectory that reaches a point of zero \
acceleration, but otherwise accelerates. All other trajectories cross the \
zero acceleration curve twice, and have once decelerated period.

First run \[OpenCurlyQuote]Set-Up\[CloseCurlyQuote], then proceed to any \
other section.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.953806782945103*^9, 3.953806796746586*^9}, {
  3.960663064442158*^9, 3.9606632951904793`*^9}, {3.960663657855912*^9, 
  3.960663690448955*^9}, {3.960663809692812*^9, 3.960663822621565*^9}, {
  3.960663964996393*^9, 3.960664050605285*^9}, {3.960664084341357*^9, 
  3.960664100324112*^9}, {3.960907694335533*^9, 3.960907747880417*^9}, {
  3.9609078919516487`*^9, 
  3.9609079027784405`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9e0ea730-8e64-b44b-ba3e-\
38d29a90cf62"],

