Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Conclusions",
 FontSize->36,
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.7607843137254902, 0.29411764705882354`, 0.08235294117647059]]], "Subtitle",\

 CellChangeTimes->{{3.89325259655807*^9, 3.893252598919417*^9}, {
  3.8932560720239463`*^9, 3.893256076743604*^9}, {3.893256115992225*^9, 
  3.893256116067061*^9}, {3.89772743676551*^9, 3.897727458937772*^9}, {
  3.937991997809936*^9, 3.937991998495105*^9}, {3.960899205049299*^9, 
  3.960899206116556*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"038cf5ce-5bf1-c543-845c-\
3fa309f0451e"],

Cell["\<\
In this notebook, we have completed a dynamical systems analysis of dark \
matter interacting with dark energy with a quadratic EoS. We wanted to \
understand if there was a range of parameters, such that all trajectories \
avoid a singularity, have a decelerated expansion phase, and tend towards a \
cosmological constant at low energy. When \[Epsilon] = -1, wx > -1, and q > \
3, we find that in the Z-X phase space all trajectories emerge from a \
non-singular repellor during expansion, have at least one decelerated \
expansion phase, and tend towards a low energy cosmological constant at \
late-times, for any initial condition. This is the case even if we set the \
parameters such that the high energy repellor is between Planck and \
inflationary energy scales, and the low energy attractor is close to the \
observed value of the cosmological constant. In the corresponding 3D phase \
space, open and flat models, as well as a subset of closed models which \
bounce once, are non-singular, and have at least one decelerated phase during \
expansion.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9607052041301174`*^9, 3.960705234219162*^9}, {
  3.960705478755558*^9, 3.9607055884387684`*^9}, {3.9609611779440804`*^9, 
  3.9609612885151176`*^9}, {3.960963002095108*^9, 
  3.96096306605995*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"753a6423-7693-3c49-be37-\
9ae97f843908"],

Cell["", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9605388650218887`*^9, 3.960538867427691*^9}, {
   3.960541143499325*^9, 3.9605411506097736`*^9}, {3.960543108010094*^9, 
   3.960543136585682*^9}, {3.960544191311695*^9, 3.960544196417282*^9}, {
